<title>USA: U.S. FAA upgrades assessment of Peru air safety.</title>
<headline>U.S. FAA upgrades assessment of Peru air safety.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Aviation Administration has upgraded Peru, finding it now meets international safety standards.</p>
<p>In November 1995, FAA rated Peru &quot;conditional&quot; after a review of the country's civil aviation authority.</p>
<p>Countries whose air carriers fly to the United States must adhere to the safety guidelines of the International Civil Aviation Organization.</p>
<p>FAA made its announcement on Peru in a statement issued late Friday.</p>
</text>
